# API integration pre-push gate (umbraculum-class monorepos)

## Two-tier pre-push (hard)

| Tier | Tool | Catches | Does **not** catch |
|------|------|---------|---------------------|
| **1 — Static analysis** | `npm run verify:pre-push` (T2-PR / skill **`path-aware-pre-push`**) | Path-resolved ci-parity jobs (TS, lint, docs, …) | Vitest runtime, Redis/BullMQ teardown, DB integration (unless T2 also starts api companion) |
| **2 — API integration** | **`api-integration-tests-pre-push`** skill (or T2 companion when `api.yml` paths match) | GHA `api` workflow failures (`npm test`, unhandled vitest rejections with `REDIS_URL`) | Playwright e2e, deploy, DNS |

When editing **`services/api/**`**, API test files, **`buildApp()`** boot paths, or shared packages in `.github/workflows/api.yml` path filters: run **both tiers** before push (T2-PR may already start the api companion — still treat vitest Unhandled Errors as FAIL).

## Rule (hard)

1. **Do not treat `docker compose exec api npm run typecheck` or a green dev UI as sufficient** for API changes.
2. **Do not treat bare `npx @umbraculum/ci-parity` alone as sufficient** for API changes — use T2-PR; it still does not replace Redis vitest when the companion did not run.
3. **Treat vitest "Tests passed" + "Unhandled Errors" / `Errors: 1` as FAIL** — CI exits non-zero the same way.
4. Procedure: skill **`path-aware-pre-push`** / `npm run verify:pre-push` for tier 1; skill **`api-integration-tests-pre-push`** when api paths are in scope and T2 did not already cover them. Rules **`72`** / **`76`**.

## Agent anti-patterns

| Anti-pattern | Why it fails |
|---|---|
| Push after only manual browser check | Misses test-file TS errors and vitest teardown |
| `vitest run` without Redis when CI sets `REDIS_URL` | Misses BullMQ/ioredis lifecycle bugs |
| Ignoring unhandled rejection summary | CI fails despite 542 passed tests |

## Runbook

Skill: `api-integration-tests-pre-push` in this plugin.
